{{!-- The field wears a drawn box, the same `box` the Gold chip wears: without it the text sat on
      bare paper with nothing to say it could be typed into, and the tab read as a paragraph
      someone had already written. The placeholder says the same thing again for an empty one.

      A thousand characters is the cap, held both here and in `_processFormData` — `maxlength`
      stops the typing and the pasting, and the submit path stops everything else. --}}
<section class="tab cairn-edit-panel {{tab.cssClass}}" data-group="primary" data-tab="bond">
    <textarea class="cairn-edit-text" name="system.bond" maxlength="{{limits.text}}"
        placeholder="{{localize 'CAIRN.Edit.BondPlaceholder'}}"
        data-ink="box" data-ink-seed="edit-bond" data-ink-w="1.6">{{system.bond}}</textarea>
</section>
